sentences.text:
The petitioner who had entered into an agreement with the 2nd respondent, for running a canteen in the office premises of the 1st respondent, has approached this Court seeking the following reliefs:-
i) To issue a writ of mandamus or any other writ, order or direction, directing the respondents to allow the petitioner to continue to the canteen on the basis of Exhibit P1 agreement;
ii) To declare that Exhibit P5 notice issued by the 2nd respondent within a span of 10 months of Exhibit P1 is illegal and unsustainable;
iii) To command the respondents to provide an opportunity to hear the side of the petitioner;
2. The challenge is against Ext.P5 notice by which the petitioner was required to stop the functioning of the canteen with effect from 18.10.2025.

